{
  "id": "murphy-shakti-60min-bilateral-mod40-fast",
  "name": "Shakti 60-min bilateral session: modulated 40 Hz (fast alternation)",
  "category": "spiritual",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (8 Coil Shakti)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "Murphy's single 60-minute session 'to try to create an intense experience in ONE session': the modulated 40 Hz signal over both temporal lobes on the 8 Coil Shakti crosses, with the two coil pairs taking turns every half-second (the vendor's fast alternation).",
  "setting": "Blindfold, earplugs or a sound-blocking headset (the vendor: 'substituting white noise won't work'), no interruptions and no plans afterwards. Murphy: 'For the first twenty minutes, not much happens.'",
  "schedule": "A one-off for a single intense experience, not a series (the vendor: repeating it 'might eventually elicit an unpleasant experience'); at most once every 3 weeks.",
  "notes": "Four coils in a cross over each temporal lobe, as in the 8 Coil Shakti chart: top C5/C6, bottom T9/T10, front FT7/FT8, back TP7/TP8. One stereo channel drives the top and bottom coils of both crosses, the other the front and back coils; the vendor says single long sessions 'should be bilateral'. The vendor's optional fast mode switches channels 'twice each second' and, it says, 'emerged as the most effective' in the original developers' lab tests; here (two tracks) the top and bottom coils and the front and back coils take turns every 0.5 s. The standard ('slow') mode switches after each instance of the signal; a constant tone has no instances, so only the fast mode is built. Coil polarity follows the vendor's chart, one + and one − coil in each pair: on the left cross the top (C5) and front (FT7) coils are − and the bottom (T9) and back (TP7) coils +; on the right cross the top (C6) and front (FT8) coils are + and the bottom (T10) and back (TP8) coils −. The − coils have negative weights, which reverse their current as if the coil were turned over; + is taken as this helmet's normal drive. The 'modulated 40 Hz' file is proprietary; the vendor describes a constant tone, calibrated at 10 mG (1 µT, the default here). It is approximated by a phase-modulated sine, a 40 Hz carrier whose phase swings up to 3 rad either way every 2 s (about 38.5-41.5 Hz), stored as 1-ms point tables so that it can be switched between the pairs. Independent double-blind tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005; Gendle & McGrath 2012). Not for people with epilepsy, seizure history or a psychiatric condition; stop on distress.",
  "targets": ["left-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior", "right-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior", "left-temporal-pole", "right-temporal-pole"],
  "source": "Murphy, Shakti demo: Two ways to use Shakti https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/two_ways.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: 60 minute sessions https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/hour.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Both temporal lobes https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/bi_temporal.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Getting started (8-coil chart; one test every 72 hours) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/getting_started_basic.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Understanding the 8 Coil Shakti (fast and slow alternation) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_principles.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: 8 coil placement https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/8_coil_placement.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Using the 8 Coil Shakti over the temporal lobes https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_temporal.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Modulated 40 Hz (obe45) signal (constant tone, 10 mG) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/obe45_consent.htm ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/ ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/ ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Overcoming dud sessions (60-min sessions every 21 days) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/duds.htm",
